    kg:textSpan "predictive entropy. Bayesian AL by disagreement (BALD) [ 10 ] and its batch version (i.e., BatchBALD) [ 12 ] instead compute the mutual information between the model predictions and the model parameters, which indeed chooses samples that maximise the decrease in expected entropy [20]. Recently, inspired by the one-step-look-ahead strategy of ELR [ 23 ], Zhao et al. [42] extended MOCU [ 39 ] to WMOCU with a theoretical guarantee of convergence. But WMOCU only applies to errors which are less rele" .

