    kg:textSpan "batch CoreMSE with different batch sizes (i.e., B { 1 , 5 , 10 , 50 , 100 } ) on PUBMED and SST-5 as an example. The curves demonstrate that the performance of smaller batch sizes (5 or 10) is superior to that of large batch sizes (50 or 100), especially in the early rounds of training, but surprisingly also superior to that of the no-batch case. The no-batch case need to perform multiple one-step-look-ahead optimising acquisitions (Algorithm 1 and Algorithm 2) sequentially in order to acquire B" .

