    kg:docId "17-2310.14230v3_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/17-2310_14230v3_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "cover-based method, tends to select outliers in the low-budget regime. In this case, cover-based AL is opposite to density-based AL, which also indicates that density-based AL may be a better choice in the low-budget regime. From the perspective of methodology, cover-based AL needs to solve an NP-hard problem in linear time with a greedy algorithm. Although this algorithm results in acceptable solutions, its almost impossible to know how the AL performance would be if the optimal solutions could" .

