    kg:textSpan "bags of the same class. The same can be said about instances in cluster b). In cluster c) and d), all labeled instances belong to the same class even if their bag labels are different. The remaining instances are therefore deemed to be uninformative. Most of the instance labels in cluster e) are known and thus, the label of the remaining instance is unlikely to provide useful information. Instances in cluster f) should be informative because there is label disagreement at bag and instance level," .

