    kg:textSpan "is potentially harmful because the positions are likely to vary for different instances of the character. A simple way to reduce the precision with which the position of distinctive features are encoded in a feature map is to reduce the spatial resolution of the feature map. This can be achieved with a so-called subsampling layer, which performs a local averaging and a subsampling, thereby reducing the resolution of the feature map and reducing the sensitivity of the output to shifts and distort" .

