    :hasEvidenceChunk "113-2111.02275v2_rag::chunk_005"^^xsd:string,
        "127-1909.03585v1_rag::chunk_016"^^xsd:string,
        "180-2205.11320v3_rag::chunk_001"^^xsd:string,
        "186-2201.11661v1_rag::chunk_009"^^xsd:string,
        "196-2011.01285v1_rag::chunk_007"^^xsd:string,
        "197-2202.01402v2_rag::chunk_001"^^xsd:string,
        "22-2203.13450v3_rag::chunk_003"^^xsd:string,
        "31-2020.emnlp-main.637_rag::chunk_003"^^xsd:string,
        "60-2022.findings-emnlp.235_rag::chunk_006"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasEvidenceText "2) uncertainty sampling, e.g. , selecting data points with high entropy, to avoid inter-iteration redundancy"^^xsd:string,
        "2) uncertainty sampling, e.g. , selecting data points with high entropy, to avoid inter-iteration redundancy."^^xsd:string,
        "Among various active learning approaches, uncertainty sampling is one of the widely used techniques"^^xsd:string,
        "An uncertainty-based method that selects samples with least condence."^^xsd:string,
        "Epistemic uncertainty comes from the modeling/learning process and is caused by a lack of knowledge"^^xsd:string,
        "Recently, it was shown that uncertainty sampling is inherently unsuited for the low-budget regime, which may explain the cold start phenomenon"^^xsd:string,
        "The most common approach to active learning is uncertainty sampling . The idea is to train a model based on an initial set of labeled data and then to select unlabeled examples that the model cannot classify with certainty."^^xsd:string,
        "The most widely used scores are the uncertainty sampling approaches, such as entropy sampling, which scores examples by s ENT , the entropy of the classier predictions"^^xsd:string,
        "two general AL strategies: uncertainty sampling and diversity sampling."^^xsd:string,
        "uncertainty sampling is inherently unsuited for the low-budget regime, which may explain the cold start phenomenon"^^xsd:string,
        "uncertainty sampling, e.g. , selecting data points with high entropy"^^xsd:string,
        "using epistemic uncertainty to identify the most informative points for label acquisition."^^xsd:string,
        "we discuss two general AL strategies: uncertainty sampling and diversity sampling."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :query_strategy,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "UncertaintySampling"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "An active learning approach where a model selects unlabeled examples that it cannot classify with certainty to be labeled and used for re-training."^^xsd:string ;
