    kg:textSpan "are designed for class-incremental setting in which a model (often a neural network) learns from training data of different classes in different increments and then evaluated on the test data of all the classes learned so far [ 3 ]. Most existing class-incremental learning (CIL) methods avoid catastrophic forgetting by storing a portion of the training samples from previous classes and retraining the model on a mixture of the stored data and new data [ 3 , 31 ]. However, this approach does not s" .

