        "28-s10994-023-06454-2_rag::chunk_009"^^xsd:string,
        "51-1910.07153v2_rag::chunk_000"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasEvidenceText "Active Learning AL is just such a method dedicated to studying how to obtain as many performance gains as possible by labeling as few samples as possible."^^xsd:string,
        "Active learning (AL) (Settles, 2009) is a framework in which learners can select data that improve the prediction accuracy."^^xsd:string,
        "Active learning (AL) combines data labeling and model training to minimize the labeling cost by prioritizing the selection of high value data"^^xsd:string,
        "Active learning can be considered a special case of semi-supervised learning, as it allows the model to actively select which data points it wants to be labeled"^^xsd:string,
        "Many works integrated existing consistency-based semi-supervised methods into the training process of AL."^^xsd:string,
        "The intelligent selection of data to be annotated can help to reach a good model performance using fewer labels. In our work the AL procedure is set in the context of image segmentation."^^xsd:string,
        "We study acquisition functions for active learning (AL) for text classication."^^xsd:string,
        "active learning (Settles, 2009) is a practical method for constructing a useful prediction model with the minimum number of annotations"^^xsd:string ;
