    kg:textSpan "transited to deep neural networks. Gal et al. (2017) used Monte-Carlo (MC) Dropout (Gal and Ghahramani, 2016) to generate posterior samples of the neural network output, based on which a variety of acquisition functions, such as predictive entropy and Bayesian Active Learning by Disagreement (BALD) (Houlsby et al., 2011), can be calculated and optimized to query new examples in active learning. This approach has been proven successful in image classication. Kirsch et al. (2019) developed BatchBA" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/107-2206_12569v1_rag__chunk_002> a kg:Chunk ;
