    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/26-2009_00236v2_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "cycle. In the initial state, we can randomly select one or more samples from the unlabeled pool , give this sample to the oracle query label to get the labeled dataset , and then train the model on using supervised learning. Next, we use this new knowledge to select the next sample to be queried, add the newly queried sample to , and then conduct training. This process is repeated until the label budget is exhausted or the pre-defined termination conditions are reached (see Section 3.4 for stopp" .

