    kg:textSpan "the cold start problem can be further aggravated. Treating samples of all classes equally often leads to selecting samples that are likely to be similar or highly correlated, and thus are not representative [20], [36]. In the LTS framework, the uncertainty of samples is measured using a regressor that is dynamically trained on samples labeled with their losses from the boosting model. If we select samples by only taking the uncertainty of samples into consideration, the cold start problem would " .

