    :hasEvidenceText "A Survey of Deep Active Learning 5 It is different from DL by using manual or"^^xsd:string,
        "Active Learning (AL) reduces labeling costs by select"^^xsd:string,
        "Active learning (AL) combines data labeling and model training to minimize the labeling cost"^^xsd:string,
        "Active learning (AL) is a label-ecient technique for training deep models when only a limited labeled set is available and the manual annotation is expensive."^^xsd:string,
        "Better and more universal enhancement methods are needed in DAL."^^xsd:string,
        "DAL algorithms, and new basic learned models. This makes the application of DAL to downstream tasks"^^xsd:string,
        "Deep Active Learning (DeepAL), an approach combining DL and AL to maximize task performance while minimizing"^^xsd:string,
        "This makes the application of DAL to downstream tasks, and designing new DAL algorithms becomes easier."^^xsd:string,
        "This section provides an overview of highly-cited DAL methods in recent years, including the perspectives of querying strategies and techniques for enhancing DAL methods."^^xsd:string,
        "While deep learning (DL) is data-hungry and usually relies on extensive labeled data to deliver good performance, Active Learning (AL) reduces labeling costs"^^xsd:string,
        "application of DAL to downstream tasks, and designing new DAL algorithms becomes easier."^^xsd:string,
        "deep active learning (DAL) starts with a random initialization."^^xsd:string,
        "existing deep active learning methods are usually designed based on heuristic criteria"^^xsd:string,
        "feature representations are dynamically changing during DAL processes"^^xsd:string,
        "to as DeepAL, was proposed by considering the complementary advantages of the two methods"^^xsd:string,
