    :hasEvidenceText "Human annotators who act as oracles"^^xsd:string,
        "Human annotators who act as oracles are usually subject to accidental mislabeling"^^xsd:string,
        "S is subsequently labeled by an oracle"^^xsd:string,
        "The subset is annotated by an oracle in semi-supervised setting and added to the training dataset"^^xsd:string,
        "We consider two types of oracles: an ideal oracle which always provides correct labels for the active learner, and a noisy oracle"^^xsd:string,
        "an ideal oracle which always provides correct labels for the active learner"^^xsd:string,
        "asks an oracle (usually a human annotator) to label a new set of points."^^xsd:string,
        "each oracle (i.e., annotator) only knows or is familiar with a small part of the problem"^^xsd:string,
        "identifying a set of data-points and presenting them to an oracle to be labelled"^^xsd:string,
        "query the oracle with an instance for the label instead of directly transfering the labels."^^xsd:string,
        "select the most useful samples from the unlabeled dataset and hand it over to the oracle (e.g., human annotator) for labeling"^^xsd:string,
        "selected and sent to the labeling experts."^^xsd:string,
        "the oracles cognitive capacity to respond to the queries as measured by memory retention"^^xsd:string,
        "we use a Gaussian process model trained by the finite element simulation datasets as an oracle model."^^xsd:string ;
