    kg:textSpan "We make assumptions 2.1 and 2.2 (consistency, and unconfoundedness). We relax assumption 2.3 (overlap) by allowing for its violation over subsets of the support of D pool . We present all theorems, proofs, and detailed assumptions in Appendix A . 3.1 How do naive acquisition functions bias the training data? To motivate CausalBALD, we rst look at a set of naive acquisition functions. A random acquisition function selects data points uniformly at random from D pool and adds them to D train . In F" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/186-2201_11661v1_rag__chunk_003> a kg:Chunk ;
