    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/186-2201_11661v1_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "y ic | x i ; t ) . In most AL approaches, a data acquisition model at time t corresponds to the trained classication model at time t 1 , i.e. , M t = t 1 . We call this monotonic acquisition , since a naive belief would be assuming the last trained model t 1 is effective enough to not only provide a good representation for the entire labeled data L but also estimate acquisition factors ( e.g. , condence) for remaining unlabeled data U . Data Acquisition Models in AL Despite the remarkable succes" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/26-2009_00236v2_rag__chunk_004> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "26-2009.00236v2_rag::chunk_004" ;
    kg:docId "26-2009.00236v2_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/26-2009_00236v2_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "urgently required. 1.2 Active Learning AL is just such a method dedicated to studying how to obtain as many performance gains as possible by labeling as few samples as possible. More specifically, it aims to select the most useful samples from the unlabeled dataset and hand it over to the oracle (e.g., human annotator) for labeling, to reduce the cost of labeling as much as possible while still maintaining performance. AL approaches can be divided into membership query synthesis [ 10 , 113 ], st" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/26-2009_00236v2_rag__chunk_021> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "26-2009.00236v2_rag::chunk_021" ;
    kg:docId "26-2009.00236v2_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/26-2009_00236v2_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "and unlabeled datasets, ARAL [ 146 ] also uses samples produced by deep production networks to jointly train the entire model. ARAL [ 146 ] comprises both VAAL [ 204 ] and adversarial representation learning [ 53 ]. By using VAAL [ 204 ] to learn the potential feature representation space of the labeled and unlabeled data, the unlabeled samples with the largest amount of information can be selected accordingly. At the same time, both real and generated data are used to enhance the models learnin" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/49-1904_00370v3_rag__chunk_006> a kg:Chunk ;
