    kg:textSpan "random variables 1: and 1: in a product probability space, and I ( 1: ; | 1: , ) denotes the mutual information between these two random variables. BatchBALD considers the correlation between different query samples by designing an explicit joint mutual information mechanism to obtain a better query batch sample set. The batch-based query strategy forms the basis of the combination of AL and DL, and related research on this topic is also very rich. We will provide a detailed overview and discuss" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/113-2111_02275v2_rag__chunk_005> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "113-2111.02275v2_rag::chunk_005" ;
    kg:docId "113-2111.02275v2_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/113-2111_02275v2_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "correct label would be. We focus on using epistemic uncertainty to identify the most informative points for label acquisition. Bayesian Active Learning by Disagreement (BALD) [ 18 ] denes an acquisition function based on epistemic uncertainty. Specically, it uses the mutual information (MI) between the unknown output and model parameters as a measure of disagreement: I(Y; | x , D train ) = H(Y | x , D train ) E p ( |D train ) [H(Y | x , )] , (1) where H is the entropy function; a straightforward" .

