    kg:textSpan "density networks to estimate a probability distribution for each localization and classication heads output for the object detection task. Revising the loss function of the target model is also promising. WAAL adopts min-max loss by leveraging the unlabeled data for better distinguishing labeled and unlabeled samples [ 63 ]. Another approach is ensemble learning. DNNs use a softmax layer to obtain the labels posterior probability and tend to be overcondent when calculating the uncertainty. To in" .

