    :hasEvidenceText "A random acquisition function selects data points uniformly at random from D pool and adds them to D train ."^^xsd:string,
        "Active learning research focuses on developing novel acquisition functions for selecting data points to be annotated by the oracle."^^xsd:string,
        "Bayesian Active Learning by Disagreement (BALD) [ 18 ] denes an acquisition function based on epistemic uncertainty."^^xsd:string,
        "To decide what data points to acquire though we used MC dropout following the derivations above."^^xsd:string,
        "To decide what data points to acquire though we used MC dropout following the derivations above. We repeated the acquisition process 100 times, each time acquiring the 10 points that maximised the acquisition function over the pool set."^^xsd:string,
        "We focus on using epistemic uncertainty to identify the most informative points for label acquisition. Bayesian Active Learning by Disagreement (BALD) [ 18 ] denes an acquisition function"^^xsd:string,
        "a data point from the unlabeled set U is selected to be labeled, according to an acquisition function A measuring the information gain of a potential data point x"^^xsd:string,
        "a variety of acquisition functions, such as predictive entropy and Bayesian Active Learning by Disagreement (BALD)"^^xsd:string,
        "acquisition functions, such as predictive entropy and Bayesian Active Learning by Disagreement (BALD) (Houlsby et al., 2011), can be calculated and optimized to query new examples in active learning."^^xsd:string,
        "an acquisition function A measuring the information gain of a potential data point x"^^xsd:string,
        "an acquisition function a ( x, M ) is a function of x that the AL system uses t"^^xsd:string,
        "maximizes the acquisition function (2) . It is often the case that a single example will not cause a signicant change of the model posterior"^^xsd:string,
        "the 10 points that maximised the acquisition function over the pool set"^^xsd:string,
        "the acquisition function must be simple to compute and optimize (e.g., distance to classication hyper-plane) because it will be used by the generative model during the sample generation process"^^xsd:string,
        "unifying the uncertainty and diversity objectives into a single acquisition function"^^xsd:string,
        "using an acquisition function to be annotated by the oracle such that the expected loss is minimized."^^xsd:string,
        "where a ( x , M ) is the acquisition function"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :method,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "Acquisition Function"^^xsd:string,
        "Acquisition function"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A function used in active learning to determine which unlabeled data points should be acquired and incorporated into the training set."^^xsd:string ;
